          "notes": "Fastned \"Model 3 Long Range (2019 - 2023)\" curve, CCS2 300 kW charger, battery around 30 C. Measured on the CCS2 port, so the plateau is capped near 195 kW (InsideEVs reports the same Fastned 2020 LR AWD at 195 kW peak / 128 kW 20-80% average); a North American Supercharger session reaches ~250 kW early (Bjorn Nyland 2019 LR AWD: 250 kW peak, 128 kW 20-80% average via InsideEVs, which agrees on the average). Curve starts at 11 % SoC and ends at 90 %. Applies to the 2017-2020 Panasonic NCA hardware; software/charger differences move the early plateau.",
